      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Express $2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{16\\pi}{11}\\right)-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{16\\pi}{11}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{16\\pi}{11}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{16\\pi}{11}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{32\\pi}{11}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
